go-to: return

@barons_split
title: SLD registers against the coordinating centre
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "barons"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= An organisation becomes a list

Leaks became a deadline, then public criticism, failed whips, individual
defections and a parliamentary circle. The regional organisation now approves
an **SLD list**. MPs still decide individually whether office, their local base,
personal following and dependence on a Lewica nomination make departure safer.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@spring_split
title: Wiosna registers a competing Spring list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "spring"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= A brand becomes a list

The free-vote threat became rebellion, individual defections and a club.
Wiosna now approves a **Spring list**, but recognisable MPs with offices or high
dependence on the common nomination can still remain with the rump.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@labor_split
title: The labour current registers its own list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "labor"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= The labour club becomes a party

After refusing the whip and losing individual MPs, the labour circle approves
an independent **Labour Left list**. Union organisation pulls some deputies
out; ministries, constituency work and list dependence hold others back.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@progressives_split
title: Young Left registers a competing list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "progressives"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= The movement enters electoral competition

The progressive rebellion has already produced resignations, defections and a
club. It now approves a **Young Left list**. Ideological intensity and personal
followings favour departure; offices and common-list dependence still divide
the MPs.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@razem_split
title: Razem leaves the common list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "razem"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= Autonomy becomes electoral competition

[? if razem_merged: Razem's former network must rebuild a legal party before it can contest the common organisation.?][? if not razem_merged: Razem's legal outside option makes the final organisational step easy.?] The decision still
does not make its estimated caucus a unitary block. Each MP weighs office,
local organisers, a personal following, ideology and dependence on the common
list before the **Razem list** is registered.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@pps_split
title: PPS registers outside the common list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "pps"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= A small circle creates another threshold

The PPS circle approves its own list. Its historic label provides an outside
option, but the decision still belongs to its individual parliamentarians.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@social_patriot_split
title: Lewica Patriotyczna registers its own list
new-page: true
on-arrival: caucus_exit_target = "social_patriot"; caucus_exit_mode = "escalated"

= The alternative Left becomes electoral

The organisation already has a name, a leadership and regional referrals.
After failed whips and a parliamentary circle, **Lewica Patriotyczna** files
its own party list. Its MPs still decide individually whether the outside route
is stronger than their offices and dependence on the common nomination.

- @resolve_exit: Continue as the Lewica coordinating centre

@resolve_exit
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const target = String(Q.caucus_exit_target || "");
const mode = String(Q.caucus_exit_mode || "orderly");
const definitions = {
    barons: {
        committee: "sld_breakaway",
        seat: "sld_breakaway_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_barons_seats",
        advisers: ["czarzasty", "wieczorek"],
        headline: "The organisational establishment refounds SLD"
    },
    spring: {
        committee: "spring_breakaway",
        seat: "spring_breakaway_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_spring_seats",
        advisers: ["biedron"],
        headline: "Wiosna restores an independent Spring party"
    },
    labor: {
        committee: "labor_left",
        seat: "labor_left_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_labor_seats",
        advisers: ["dziemianowicz_bak"],
        headline: "The labour current forms an independent Labour Left"
    },
    progressives: {
        committee: "young_left",
        seat: "young_left_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_progressives_seats",
        advisers: ["zukowska", "kotula", "gawkowski", "nowicka"],
        headline: "The progressive current launches Young Left"
    },
    razem: {
        committee: "razem",
        seat: "razem_party_seats",
        internalSeat: "razem_seats",
        advisers: ["zandberg", "biejat", "zawisza"].concat(
            Q.social_patriot_active ? [] : ["matysiak"]
        ),
        headline: "Razem leaves the common caucus"
    },
    pps: {
        committee: "pps",
        seat: "pps_party_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_pps_seats",
        advisers: ["konieczny", "morawska_stanecka", "kwiatkowski"],
        headline: "PPS forms a separate parliamentary and electoral circle"
    },
    social_patriot: {
        committee: "social_patriot",
        seat: "social_patriot_seats",
        internalSeat: "left_social_patriot_seats",
        advisers: ["matysiak"],
        headline: "Lewica Patriotyczna leaves the common Left"
    }
};
const definition = definitions[target];
if (
    definition &&
    Q[target + "_active"] &&
    !(target == "razem" && Q.razem_breakaway_protected)
) {
    const activeLeftCaucuses = [
        "barons",
        "spring",
        "labor",
        "progressives",
        "razem",
        "pps",
        "social_patriot"
    ].filter(function(caucus) {
        if (caucus == "razem" && Q.razem_breakaway_protected) {
            return false;
        }
        return Q[caucus + "_active"] && Q[caucus + "_in_left"];
    }).length;
    const strength = Math.max(
        0.5,
        Number(Q[target + "_strength"]) || 0
    );
    const currentLeftSeats = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)
    );
    const recordedSeats = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q[definition.internalSeat]) || 0)
    );
    const proportionalSeats = currentLeftSeats > 0
        ? Math.max(1, Math.round(currentLeftSeats * strength / 100))
        : 0;
    const availableSeats = Math.min(
        currentLeftSeats,
        recordedSeats > 0 ? recordedSeats : proportionalSeats
    );
    const priorIndividualDefections = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q[target + "_individual_defections"]) || 0)
    );
    const estimatedCaucusMps = Math.max(
        priorIndividualDefections + availableSeats,
        Math.round(Number(Q[target + "_estimated_mps"]) || 0)
    );
    const officeHold = Math.min(
        100,
        (Number(Q[target + "_office_hold"]) || 0) +
            (Q.left_in_government ? 8 : 0)
    );
    const localOrganisation =
        Number(Q[target + "_local_organisation"]) || 0;
    const personalFollowing =
        Number(Q[target + "_personal_following"]) || 0;
    const ideologicalIntensity =
        Number(Q[target + "_ideological_intensity"]) || 0;
    const listDependence =
        Number(Q[target + "_list_dependence"]) || 0;
    const brokerCohesion = Number(Q[target + "_cohesion"]) || 0;
    const grievanceMemory =
        Number(Q[target + "_grievance_memory"]) || 0;
    const lateCaucusExitScale = activeLeftCaucuses <= 1
        ? 0.12
        : (activeLeftCaucuses == 2
            ? 0.35
            : (activeLeftCaucuses == 3 ? 0.70 : 1));
    const departureFloor = activeLeftCaucuses <= 1
        ? 0.01
        : (activeLeftCaucuses == 2 ? 0.05 : 0.18);
    const departureCeiling = activeLeftCaucuses <= 1
        ? 0.22
        : (activeLeftCaucuses == 2 ? 0.40 : 0.82);
    const departureRate = Math.max(
        departureFloor,
        Math.min(
            departureCeiling,
            (
                0.10 +
                    localOrganisation * 0.0022 +
                    personalFollowing * 0.0017 +
                    ideologicalIntensity * 0.0022 +
                    brokerCohesion * 0.0013 +
                    grievanceMemory * 0.001 +
                    (100 - listDependence) * 0.0015 -
                    officeHold * 0.002
            ) * lateCaucusExitScale
        )
    );
    const maximumFinalWave = estimatedCaucusMps > 1
        ? Math.max(0, availableSeats - 1)
        : availableSeats;
    const minimumExitSeats = activeLeftCaucuses <= 2 ? 0 : 1;
    const exitSeats = availableSeats > 0
        ? Math.min(
            currentLeftSeats,
            maximumFinalWave,
            Math.max(
                minimumExitSeats,
                Math.round(availableSeats * departureRate)
            )
        )
        : 0;
    const totalDeparted = priorIndividualDefections + exitSeats;

    Q[target + "_exit_strength"] = strength * departureRate;
    Q[target + "_mp_departure_rate"] = departureRate;
    Q[target + "_mp_departed"] = totalDeparted;
    Q[target + "_mp_retained"] = Math.max(
        0,
        estimatedCaucusMps - totalDeparted
    );
    Q[target + "_active"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_in_left"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_party_formed"] = 1;
    if (target == "pps") {
        Q.rozenek_in_left = 0;
        Q.morawska_stanecka_in_left = 0;
    }
    Q[target + "_party_relation"] =
        mode == "punitive" ? 8 : (mode == "escalated" ? 18 : 45);
    Q[target + "_last_crisis_time"] = Number(Q.time) || 0;
    Q[target + "_strength"] = 0;
    Q[target + "_dissent"] = 100;
    Q.left_seats = Math.max(0, currentLeftSeats - exitSeats);
    Q[definition.seat] =
        Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q[definition.seat]) || 0)) +
        exitSeats;
    Q[definition.internalSeat] = 0;
    for (const adviser of definition.advisers) {
        Q[adviser + "_advisor"] = 0;
    }
    Q.party_unity -= mode == "punitive" ? 9 : 5;
    Q.left_poll_momentum -= mode == "punitive" ? 0.45 : 0.30;
    Q.public_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 2 : 1;

    if (target == "barons") {
        Q.local_network -= mode == "punitive" ? 12 : 6;
        Q.resources -= mode == "punitive" ? 2 : 1;
        Q.barons_party_name = "SLD";
        Q.left_party_name = "New Left Renewal";
    } else if (target == "spring") {
        Q.media_capacity -= mode == "punitive" ? 9 : 4;
        Q.progressive_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
        Q.feminist_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 4 : 1;
    } else if (target == "labor") {
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 12 : 6;
        Q.workers_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 3;
        Q.public_sector_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 4 : 2;
        if (mode == "punitive") {
            Q.member_dues = Math.max(1, (Number(Q.member_dues) || 2) - 1);
        }
    } else if (target == "progressives") {
        Q.feminist_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 10 : 5;
        Q.young_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 3;
        Q.local_network -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 2;
        Q.movement_autonomy += mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
    } else if (target == "razem") {
        Q.razem_split = 1;
        Q.razem_in_left_club = 0;
        Q.razem_opposition_circle = 1;
        Q.razem_cooperation -= mode == "punitive" ? 30 : 15;
        Q.organiser_energy -= mode == "punitive" ? 8 : 4;
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
    } else if (target == "pps") {
        Q.pps_circle_relation =
            mode == "punitive" ? 8 : (mode == "escalated" ? 18 : 45);
        Q.labor_credibility -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 2;
        Q.public_trust -= mode == "punitive" ? 3 : 1;
    } else if (target == "social_patriot") {
        Q.rural_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 2;
        Q.pensioner_support -= mode == "punitive" ? 4 : 2;
        Q.local_network -= mode == "punitive" ? 6 : 3;
        Q.matysiak_party = "Lewica Patriotyczna";
        Q.matysiak_status = "Leader of Lewica Patriotyczna";
    }
    if (Q.left_in_government) {
        const externalRazemDeparture =
            target == "razem" &&
            (
                !Q.razem_in_government ||
                String(Q.left_cabinet_model || "").includes(
                    "Razem external"
                )
            );
        if (!externalRazemDeparture) {
            Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats = Math.max(
                0,
                (Number(Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats) || 0) - exitSeats
            );
        }
        // poland_normalize derives coalition_seats once from the live cabinet
        // parties and the already-reduced left_seats value.
        Q.government_coalition_dissent +=
            mode == "punitive" ? 5 : 3;
    }
    Q.seat_subvention_seats = Q.left_seats;
    Q.seat_subvention = Q.left_seats > 0
        ? Math.max(1, Math.round(Q.left_seats / 25))
        : 0;
    Q.party_income =
        Math.max(0, Number(Q.member_dues) || 0) +
        Q.seat_subvention;
    Q.news_headline = definition.headline +
        (mode == "punitive"
            ? " after expulsions"
            : (mode == "escalated" ? " after a staged rupture" : " by agreement")) +
        "; " + totalDeparted + " MPs leave and " +
        Q[target + "_mp_retained"] + " remain";
}
Q.caucus_exit_target = "";
Q.caucus_exit_mode = "";
!}
go-to: return

@return
new-page: true
call: poland_normalize
go-to: poland_legacy_event_desk if poland_legacy_event_phase = 1; poland_event_queue if poland_event_phase = 1 and poland_legacy_event_phase = 0; poland_polling if poland_event_phase = 0 and poland_legacy_event_phase = 0
